## Architecture: Clean Architecture + DDD

### Layer Structure

```
src/
├── Domain/                          # Core Business Logic
│   ├── {Module}/
│   │   ├── Entities/                # Domain Entities (pure PHP)
│   │   │   └── {Entity}.php
│   │   ├── ValueObjects/            # Immutable Value Objects
│   │   │   └── {ValueObject}.php
│   │   ├── Services/                # Domain Services
│   │   │   └── {DomainService}.php
│   │   ├── Repositories/            # Repository Interfaces
│   │   │   └── {Entity}RepositoryInterface.php
│   │   ├── Exceptions/              # Domain Exceptions
│   │   │   └── {Domain}Exception.php
│   │   └── Rules/                   # Business Rule Objects
│   │       └── {Rule}.php
│   └── Shared/
│       ├── ValueObjects/
│       └── Exceptions/
│
├── Application/                     # Use Cases & Application Services
│   ├── {Module}/
│   │   ├── UseCases/
│   │   │   ├── {Action}{Entity}UseCase.php
│   │   │   └── {Action}{Entity}Handler.php
│   │   ├── DTOs/
│   │   │   ├── {Entity}Data.php
│   │   │   └── {Entity}Result.php
│   │   ├── Services/
│   │   │   └── {Application}Service.php
│   │   └── Ports/                   # Input/Output interfaces
│   │       ├── Input/
│   │       └── Output/
│   └── Shared/
│       └── DTOs/
│
├── Infrastructure/                  # External Implementations
│   ├── Persistence/
│   │   ├── Eloquent/
│   │   │   ├── Models/              # Eloquent Models
│   │   │   │   └── {Entity}Model.php
│   │   │   └── Repositories/        # Repository Implementations
│   │   │       └── Eloquent{Entity}Repository.php
│   │   └── Mappers/
│   │       └── {Entity}Mapper.php
│   ├── Cache/
│   │   └── Redis{Entity}Cache.php
│   ├── Queue/
│   │   └── Jobs/
│   ├── Mail/
│   ├── External/                    # Third-party integrations
│   └── Logging/
│
└── Interface/                       # HTTP/CLI Layer
    ├── Http/
    │   ├── Controllers/
    │   │   └── {Module}/
    │   │       └── {Entity}Controller.php
    │   ├── Requests/
    │   │   └── {Module}/
    │   │       └── {Action}{Entity}Request.php
    │   ├── Resources/
    │   │   └── {Module}/
    │   │       └── {Entity}Resource.php
    │   └── Middleware/
    ├── Routes/
    └── Console/
```

---

## Coding Standards

### PHP Strict Mode

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);
```

**MUST** be present in every PHP file.

### PSR-12 Compliance

- Follow PSR-12 coding style strictly
- Use proper namespace declarations
- Use proper import statements (no unused imports)
- Proper indentation (4 spaces)

### Naming Conventions

```yaml
classes: PascalCase
methods: camelCase
properties: camelCase
constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
database_columns: snake_case
api_fields: snake_case
routes: kebab-case (plural nouns)
```

---

## SOLID Principles Enforcement

### Single Responsibility

```php
// ❌ BAD: Controller doing too much
class UserController
{
    public function store(Request $request)
    {
        $validated = $request->validate([...]);
        $user = User::create($validated);
        Mail::send(new WelcomeEmail($user));
        Log::info('User created');
        return response()->json($user);
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Controller delegates to UseCase
class UserController
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CreateUserUseCase $createUserUseCase
    ) {}

    public function store(CreateUserRequest $request): JsonResponse
    {
        $result = $this->createUserUseCase->execute(
            CreateUserData::fromRequest($request)
        );

        return UserResource::make($result)
            ->response()
            ->setStatusCode(Response::HTTP_CREATED);
    }
}
```

### Open/Closed Principle

```php
// Use interfaces and abstractions
interface PaymentGatewayInterface
{
    public function charge(Money $amount, PaymentMethod $method): PaymentResult;
}

class StripePaymentGateway implements PaymentGatewayInterface { }
class PayPalPaymentGateway implements PaymentGatewayInterface { }
```

### Liskov Substitution

All implementations must be substitutable for their interfaces without breaking behavior.

### Interface Segregation

```php
// ❌ BAD: Fat interface
interface UserRepositoryInterface
{
    public function find(int $id): ?User;
    public function save(User $user): void;
    public function delete(int $id): void;
    public function generateReport(): Report;
    public function sendNotification(): void;
}

// ✅ GOOD: Segregated interfaces
interface UserReadRepositoryInterface
{
    public function find(UserId $id): ?User;
    public function findByEmail(Email $email): ?User;
}

interface UserWriteRepositoryInterface
{
    public function save(User $user): void;
    public function delete(UserId $id): void;
}
```

### Dependency Inversion

```php
// Always depend on abstractions
class CreateUserUseCase
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly UserRepositoryInterface $userRepository,
        private readonly EventDispatcherInterface $eventDispatcher,
        private readonly LoggerInterface $logger
    ) {}
}
```

