## Security Requirements

### Input Validation

- ALL inputs MUST be validated via FormRequest
- Use strict type validation
- Sanitize where necessary

### SQL Injection Prevention

- Use Eloquent ORM / Query Builder
- Never use raw queries with user input
- Use parameter binding when raw queries needed

### Mass Assignment Protection

```php
// ❌ BAD
$model->fill($request->all());

// ✅ GOOD
$model->fill($request->validated());
// Or use explicit fillable in model
```

### Sensitive Data Protection

- Never log passwords, tokens, or PII
- Hash passwords with bcrypt/argon2
- Don't expose internal IDs in error messages

### Rate Limiting

```php
// routes/api.php
Route::middleware(['auth:sanctum', 'throttle:60,1'])->group(function () {
    // API routes
});
```

---

## Performance Requirements

### Eager Loading (Prevent N+1)

```php
// ❌ BAD: N+1 query
$employees = Employee::all();
foreach ($employees as $employee) {
    echo $employee->office->name; // N queries
}

// ✅ GOOD: Eager loading
$employees = Employee::with(['office', 'department', 'position'])->get();
```

### Pagination

```php
// Always paginate large datasets
$employees = EmployeeModel::query()
    ->with(['office', 'department'])
    ->orderBy('created_at', 'desc')
    ->paginate(15);
```

### Chunking for Batch Processing

```php
EmployeeModel::query()
    ->where('status', 'active')
    ->chunk(1000, function ($employees) {
        foreach ($employees as $employee) {
            // Process
        }
    });
```

### Caching

```php
// Cache expensive queries
$summary = Cache::tags(['payroll', 'reports'])
    ->remember(
        "payroll:summary:{$companyId}:{$month}:{$year}",
        now()->addHours(24),
        fn() => $this->calculateSummary($companyId, $month, $year)
    );

// Invalidate cache
Cache::tags(['payroll'])->flush();
```

### Index Recommendations

```sql
-- Always index
ALTER TABLE employees ADD INDEX idx_employees_office_status (office_id, status);
ALTER TABLE employees ADD INDEX idx_employees_email (email);
ALTER TABLE employees ADD INDEX idx_employees_code (code);

-- Composite indexes for common queries
ALTER TABLE payroll_details ADD INDEX idx_payroll_emp_period (employee_id, month, year);
ALTER TABLE trips ADD INDEX idx_trips_driver_status (driver_id, status);
```

